<labwc_config>

  <!-- No touch calibration here on purpose - see project history. The
       initial symptom (tapping Nav's bottom reveal strip didn't work, even
       though gesture-relative interactions like pinch-zoom did) looked like
       the classic "display rotated via wlr-randr but touch input wasn't"
       problem. Tried 90deg CW, 90deg CCW, and a computed 45deg CCW
       calibrationMatrix in turn, testing each on the real hardware - none
       were right, and the final measurement (90deg further CCW on top of
       the 90deg CW matrix) nets out to 0deg. So the touch digitizer was
       already reporting correctly-rotated coordinates the whole time; the
       calibration attempts were themselves the problem, not the fix. The
       real bug was something else (see Nav.tsx/touch-action history in
       app/globals.sass) - if taps ever misbehave again, don't reach for a
       calibrationMatrix first. -->

</labwc_config>
